1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,539
The passive of every tense follows the same logic: be carries the tense, and the past participle never changes.

2
00:00:07,539 --> 00:00:09,830
He writes: a letter is written.

3
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:12,604
He is writing: a letter is being written.

4
00:00:12,604 --> 00:00:15,039
He has written: has been written.

5
00:00:15,039 --> 00:00:16,861
He wrote: was written.

6
00:00:16,861 --> 00:00:19,114
He was writing: was being written.

7
00:00:19,114 --> 00:00:21,406
He had written: had been written.

8
00:00:21,406 --> 00:00:23,424
He will write: will be written.

9
00:00:23,424 --> 00:00:25,638
He must write: must be written.

10
00:00:25,638 --> 00:00:28,424
And he must have written: it must have been written.

